# Web Content Standards

- Prefer product-first language over personal branding on public pages.
- Keep copy concise and concrete; avoid unverified claims.
- Maintain working relative paths for static assets and links.
- Preserve reusable placeholders in invoice/proposal templates.
- Keep HTML/CSS static-first unless dynamic behavior is explicitly requested.
